# Request for Proposal (RFP)

## Ground Control Station Software Development Project

### RFP Number: IGCS-2025-003

---

## 1. Executive Summary

We are soliciting proposals for the development of a next-generation Integrated Ground Control Station (IGCS) software platform. This advanced software system will serve as the primary human interface for mission planning, execution, and monitoring of unmanned systems operations, providing intuitive controls for novice operators while delivering powerful capabilities for advanced users and multi-vehicle swarm operations.

## 2. Project Overview

The IGCS software will deliver a comprehensive command and control interface for unmanned systems, with capabilities spanning from basic flight controls to complex swarm operations. The system will incorporate real-time data analytics, adaptive control interfaces, and intelligent mission planning tools, while maintaining ease of use across varying skill levels.

## 3. Scope of Work

### 3.1 Core Requirements

- Develop a modular, plugin-based software architecture
- Create an adaptive user interface that scales based on operation complexity
- Implement multi-level access controls catering to different user expertise levels
- Design and build a 3D visualization engine for individual and swarm operations
- Develop contextual command suggestions based on operational context
- Create automated mission planning tools with optimization capabilities
- Implement real-time telemetry processing and visualization
- Develop operational efficiency metrics and analysis tools
- Create performance optimization recommendations based on operational data
- Ensure compatibility with the Brain Controller Hub (BCH) and all unmanned system types

### 3.2 Technical Specifications

- Development Framework: Cross-platform (Windows, macOS, Linux)
- Programming Languages: Modern object-oriented languages (e.g., C++, Python, Java)
- 3D Engine: High-performance rendering with support for large-scale environments
- Database: Scalable solution for telemetry storage and mission archives
- Communication: Support for encrypted communications with the BCH
- Extensibility: Well-documented API for plugin development
- Deployment: Containerized deployment options for simplified installation

### 3.3 Performance Requirements

- Startup time: < 10 seconds on reference hardware
- Map rendering: 60 fps for 3D visualizations on reference hardware
- Telemetry processing: Support for 100+ data streams at 10Hz
- Simultaneous system control: Up to 50 unmanned systems
- Latency: < 100ms from control input to visualization update
- Reliability: 99.9% uptime during operations

## 4. Deliverables

1. Complete source code with comprehensive documentation
2. User interface design specifications and assets
3. Database schema and data management documentation
4. API documentation for third-party integration and plugin development
5. Comprehensive test suite and validation reports
6. User manuals for different skill levels (basic, intermediate, advanced)
